/// A module with one `private` and one `public` function.
///
/// `private` is written explicitly and is load-bearing: spec Q7 (decided
/// 2026-08-04) makes a top-level declaration PUBLIC by default, so a probe
/// that leaves the keyword off tests nothing at all.
![config(testing)]
namespace ResolutionTripwire::Vault;

/// Must NOT be callable from another module. It is. See tripwire_test.cryo.
private function secret() -> i32 { return 99; }

/// The control: a genuinely public sibling. If `secret` ever stops being
/// callable cross-module for some reason unrelated to visibility, this must
/// keep working -- otherwise the tripwire fired for the wrong reason.
public function door() -> i32 { return 1; }
